     "The study measures the presence and timing of a record, not whether the defect is covered or the notice was effective. A late entry can still be followed by a timely notice or a valid claim. Those questions need a review of the source document and the responsible lawyer. Keep the timing result separate from the legal question.",
     "The window may include a project closeout, a staff change, or a system migration that affects entries. If the process changed during the period, the items may not be comparable. Record those limits with the result and keep the source extracts. A later review should know which conditions applied.",
     "The study cannot establish that a missing entry caused a loss or a missed warranty period. It also cannot decide whether the firm met a professional duty. A record observation is an administrative finding, not a legal conclusion. The responsible lawyer should review any item with an unclear record.",
     "The sample is local and should not be generalized to other firms, projects, or jurisdictions. A different project or contract mix can produce a different result on the same day. Report the sample size and the definitions with the result. The reader should be able to judge whether the setting resembles their own."
